IMPORT policy

-- Standing preamble applied to every query below (per fixtures/queries-blind.md):
-- "Assuming all other conditions are met and no other exclusions apply
-- (where by 'other' I mean anything not referenced in the query that
-- follows)", and the agreement has been signed and the premium has been
-- paid on time. Accordingly every field of Claim not mentioned by a given
-- question is set to a value that satisfies that condition / avoids that
-- exclusion.

§ `Q1 - firefighter burns`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while doing
-- my duty as a firefighter?"
-- Burns are an accidental injury; they arose directly out of the claimant's
-- service as a fire fighter, so §3.1(3) excludes the claim.
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 30
    `nature of medical event`                            IS `Accidental Injury`
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS TRUE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 1
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q1

§ `Q2 - age 78`

-- "will my policy apply if I am 78 years old at the time of hospitalization?"
-- 78 is below the §3.1(5) threshold of 80; nothing else is referenced, so
-- the event is an ordinary, non-excluded qualifying event.
q2 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 78
    `nature of medical event`                            IS Sickness
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 1
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q2

§ `Q3 - pneumonia at 5 months, age 65`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for pneumonia 5 months after
-- the policy's effective date, and my age at the time of hospitalization is
-- 65?"
-- Pneumonia is a sickness; 65 is below the age exclusion; 5 months is well
-- inside the one-year term and the §1.3 deadline, and the wellness visit is
-- not referenced by this query so it is taken as timely.
q3 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 65
    `nature of medical event`                            IS Sickness
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 5
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q3

§ `Q4 - fall abroad, late wellness confirmation`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to a fall while traveling
-- abroad and I had given confirmation of my wellness visit 8 months after
-- the policy's effective date?"
-- Confirmation at month 8 is later than the §1.3 deadline of month 7, so the
-- condition was not satisfied in a timely fashion and the policy is
-- cancelled under §1.2 regardless of where the hospitalization occurred.
-- Hospitalizing abroad also fails the separate §2.2 "hospital in the United
-- States" requirement on these facts (see NOTES.md for the judgement call).
q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 30
    `nature of medical event`                            IS `Accidental Injury`
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS FALSE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 8
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 8
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q4

§ `Q5 - self-inflicted punch`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for punching my own face to
-- show off for my friends and I did not commit fraud or misrepresentation?"
-- No fraud/misrepresentation, so §1.2 does not cancel the policy on that
-- ground. But a deliberate punch thrown at oneself is not an "accidental"
-- injury (see NOTES.md), so the claim does not meet the basic §2.1 coverage
-- grant in the first place.
q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 30
    `nature of medical event`                            IS `Accidental Injury`
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS TRUE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 1
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q5

§ `Q6 - skydiving injury, age 79`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to an injury sustained
-- while skydiving, my age at the time of hospitalization was 79, and proof
-- of my wellness visit was provided 6.5 months after the policy's effective
-- date?"
-- The injury arose directly out of skydiving, so §3.1(1) excludes the claim
-- outright -- independent of age (79 is under 80) and of the wellness-visit
-- timing (6.5 months is inside the deadline either way).
q6 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 79
    `nature of medical event`                            IS `Accidental Injury`
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS TRUE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 6.5
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 6.5
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q6

§ `Q7 - heart attack, age 75`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for a heart attack, proof of
-- the wellness visit was submitted 2 months after the policy's effective
-- date, and my age at the time of hospitalization was 75?"
-- A heart attack is a sickness; 75 is under the age threshold; wellness
-- confirmation at month 2 is well inside the §1.3 deadline.
q7 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 75
    `nature of medical event`                            IS Sickness
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 2
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 2
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q7

§ `Q8 - military training injury`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized after being injured in a
-- military training exercise, the hospitalization occurred within the
-- policy term, and I did not commit fraud?"
-- The injury arose directly out of service in the military (a training
-- exercise is part of that service), so §3.1(2) excludes the claim, even
-- though the hospitalization is timely and there is no fraud.
q8 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 30
    `nature of medical event`                            IS `Accidental Injury`
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS TRUE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 6
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q8

§ `Q9 - son's bite, serving as a police officer`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to my son biting me in
-- the ankle, proof of my wellness visit was provided 6 months after the
-- effective date, and I was serving as a police officer at the time of
-- hospitalization?"
-- Being on duty as a police officer AT THE TIME of the injury is not the
-- same as the injury ARISING OUT OF that service (see NOTES.md): a bite
-- from the claimant's own son has no causal connection to police work, so
-- §3.1(4) does not apply. Wellness confirmation at month 6 is timely.
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS 30
    `nature of medical event`                            IS `Accidental Injury`
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS FALSE
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS FALSE
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS FALSE
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS FALSE
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS TRUE
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS 1
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS JUST 6
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q9
